--------------------------------------FILE SYSTEM TYPES AND MOUNT POINTS-------------------------------------------------------
|                                                                                                                              |
| Filesystem   | Common use             | Example mount point                      | Key thing to know                         |
| ------------ | ---------------------- | ---------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| **ext4**     | Linux general-purpose  | `/`, `/home`, `/var`                     | Very common Linux filesystem              |
| **XFS**      | Linux servers          | `/`, `/home`, `/var`                     | Common in enterprise/RHEL systems         |
| **Btrfs**    | Linux                  | `/`, `/home`                             | Snapshots & subvolumes                    |
| **ZFS**      | Servers/storage        | `/`, `/home`, `/data`                    | Advanced storage & snapshots              |
| **NTFS**     | Windows                | `C:` in Windows; `/mnt/windows` in Linux | Main Windows filesystem                   |
| **FAT32**    | USB/removable media    | `/media/user/USB`                        | Very compatible; 4 GB max file size       |
| **exFAT**    | USB/SD/removable media | `/media/user/USB`                        | Good for large files & cross-platform use |
| **ISO 9660** | CDs/DVDs               | `/media/user/CD`                         | Optical-disc filesystem                   |
